<title>USA: Canada's Martin sees strong job creation in 1997.</title>
<headline>Canada's Martin sees strong job creation in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Finance Minister Paul Martin said on Friday that signs point to strong job creation in Canada for 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;The indicators are that we are going to have quite strong job creation throughout this year,&quot; said Martin, responding to reporters' questions after a speech hosted by the Canadian Society of New York.</p>
<p>Asked if the level of the Canadian dollar was hurting Canadian competitiveness, Martin said, &quot;No, I don't think we've seen any evidence of that.&quot;</p>
<p>((-- N.A. Treasury Desk 212-859-1660))</p>
